      <span style="background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12); color: #10b981; border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Sardarshahar</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The destination delivery handover for a Two‑Wheeler or Motorcycle is a critical checkpoint that guarantees the vehicle arrives in the condition promised at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By following a structured three‑step process—daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification against the LR bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off—both the logistics provider and the recipient can confirm that the handover is accurate, transparent, and legally documented.</span></li></ul>

<h3>1. Daylight Condition Re‑inspection Against Pickup Photos</h3>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Purpose:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">To verify that the vehicle’s exterior and visible components have not suffered new damage or wear during transit.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Procedure:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The receiving party conducts a thorough visual inspection under natural daylight, comparing the vehicle side‑by‑side with the high‑resolution pickup photographs taken at the origin.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Documentation:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Any discrepancies are photographed, noted, and attached to the handover report before proceeding.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>2. Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> To ensure the mileage recorded at the point of origin matches the mileage at delivery, preventing mileage fraud.</li>
<li><strong>Procedure:</strong> The odometer reading displayed on the instrument cluster is read and recorded by both the driver and the recipient.</li>
<li><strong>Cross‑Check:</strong> This reading is compared with the mileage documented on the LR bilty (Lorry Receipt) and the pickup log.</li>
<li><strong>Outcome:</strong> If the readings align, the mileage is stamped as “verified.” Any variance triggers an investigation and is logged in the handover sheet.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Signed Condition Sign‑off</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> To create a legally binding acknowledgment that the vehicle was received in the documented condition.</li>
<li><strong>Process:</strong> The recipient reviews the inspection checklist, confirms the odometer verification, and signs the condition report.</li>
<li><strong>Components of the Sign‑off:</strong>
